metadata
    Title : Transfer State Machine Diagram
    Author : Leon Starr
    Document ID : mint.elevator3.td.5
    Modification date : Aug 5, 2026
    Version : 3.6.0
    Organization : Model Integration, LLC
    Copyright notice > MIT
    Organization logo > mint
domain Elevator Management
class Transfer
interaction events
    Execute
    Dest change request
    Ready to go
    Cabin redirected
    Cabin at destination
    Requests cleared
    Door closed
completion events
    Wait for cabin
    Cabin dispatched
    Stationary update
    Redirect requested
    Update in motion
    Reversal checked
    Call in progress
    Wait to clear
--
initial transitions
    Execute > WAITING FOR CABIN
--
state WAITING FOR CABIN
activity
    New transfer -> /R53/Cabin
    Set destination( dest: Destination floor ) -> ~UI
transitions
    Ready to go > Dispatching cabin
    Dest change request > Changing destination before cabin moves
ignore
    Door closed
        <Door closing not relevant yet> Doors may open and close while waiting to hear back
        from the Cabin. But we don’t care about closing unless we are waiting for floor
        service to expire after arrival.
can't happen
    Execute
        <Execute only from creating shaft state> Execute event is sent from same state of
        Shaft that creates the Transfer. So this event can’t happen unless a whole new
        Transfer is created.
    Dest change request
        Execute event is sent from same state of Shaft that creates the Transfer. This event
        is also sent from Shaft, in a future state, so it will always be detected after
        transitioning out of this state.
    Cabin redirected
        <Cabin not directed to move yet> Cabin hasn’t been directed to move yet.
    Ready to go
        Cabin hasn’t yet been directed to the state where this event would be sent.
    Cabin at destination
        <Cabin not directed to move yet>
    Requests cleared
        <Requests not yet cleared> We haven’t yet tried to clear any stop or floor call
        requests yet, and they can’t clear themselves alone. (Even an administration clear
        would have to first delete this instance of transfer).
--
state Changing destination before cabin moves( new dest: Level Name )
activity
    // The cabin isn’t moving, so we can safely
    // relink to the new destination
    Destination floor = ^new dest
    Stationary update -> me
transitions
    Stationary update > WAITING FOR CABIN
--
state Dispatching cabin
activity
    Go -> /R53/Cabin
    Cabin dispatched -> me
transitions
    Cabin dispatched > CABIN IN MOTION
--
state CABIN IN MOTION
activity
    // Cabin in transit
transitions
    Dest change request > Request redirect
    Cabin redirected > Match new destination of cabin
    Cabin at destination > Check for cabin reversal
can't happen
    Execute
        <Execute only from creating shaft state>
    Ready to go
        The Cabin has already reported this and cannot get back to a state where it can
        report it again without direction from this instance of Transfer, which won’t
        be triggered.
    Door closed
        The doors cannot be open when a cabin is moving. So, if we hear that they are
        just closed in this state, something has gone very wrong!
    Requests cleared
        <Requests not yet cleared>
--
state Request redirect( new dest: Level Name )
activity
    Try redirect( ^new dest ) -> /R53/Cabin
    Redirect requested -> me
transitions
    Redirect requested > CABIN IN MOTION
--
state Match new destination of cabin( updated dest: Level Name )
activity
    Destination floor = ^updated dest
    Update in motion -> me
transitions
    Update in motion > CABIN IN MOTION
--
state Check for cabin reversal
activity
    // If the Cabin arrives and there is a floor request in the opposite direction
    // and no stop request or call in the Cabin’s current travel direction,
    // we must reverse the cabin’s travel direction

    call behind .= /R53/R49/Floor Service( Direction: /R53/Cabin.Travel direction.opposite )
    call fwd .= /R53/R49/Floor Service( Direction: /R53/Cabin.Travel direction )
    switch dir = (call behind and !call fwd and !/R53/Accessible Shaft Level.Stop requested)
    switch dir? /R53/Cabin.Travel direction.toggle

    Reversal checked -> me
transitions
    Reversal checked > Check for active floor service
--
state Check for active floor service
activity
    UI.Cabin arrived( Shaft, direction: /R53/Cabin.Travel direction )
    pending floor service .= /R53/R49/Floor Service( Direction: /R53/Cabin.Travel direction )

    pending floor service? {
        Call in progress -> meCabin
        Cabin arrived -> pending floor service
    } : {
        Serviced stop -> /R53/Accessible Shaft Level
        Wait to clear -> me
    }
transitions
    Call in progress > CALL IN PROGRESS
    Wait to clear > WAITING FOR REQUESTS TO CLEAR
--
state CALL IN PROGRESS
activity
transitions
    Door closed > Canceling floor service
ignore
    Dest change request
        <Cannot redirect now> Shaft may have picked a destination, but we can’t go there
        now. We will retrigger the search when this Transfer is deleted, so there is no
        danger of missing a request.
can't happen
    Execute
        <Execute only from creating shaft state>
    Cabin redirected
        <Cabin not moving now> This event can only be sent from the cabin when it is
        moving. But it can’t be moving in this state.
    Ready to go
        <Cabin has finished moving> This event can only be sent from the cabin just before
        it begins moving. And it can’t advance beyond that without direction from this
        instance. At this point the cabin has finished moving.
    Cabin at destination
        <Cabin already arrived> The cabin has already arrived.
    Requests cleared
        <Requests not yet cleared>
--
state Canceling floor service
activity
    Cancel -> /R53/R49/Floor Service( Direction: /R53/Cabin.Travel direction )
    Wait to clear -> me
transitions
    Wait to clear > WAITING FOR REQUESTS TO CLEAR
--
state WAITING FOR REQUESTS TO CLEAR
activity
    // Requests still pending
transitions
    Requests cleared > Delete
ignore
    Dest change request
        <Cannot redirect now>
    Door closed
        Not likely to happen, but we just don’t care at this point. There is no critical
        synchronization with the door once the call in progress has been canceled.
can't happen
    Execute
        <Execute only from creating shaft state>
    Cabin redirected
        <Cabin not moving now>
    Ready to go
        <Cabin has finished moving>
    Cabin at destination
        <Cabin already arrived>
--
state Delete !*
activity
    Transfer completed -> R53( Shaft )
--